{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00578",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 7.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Hello. Just checking, you're Imani Okafor, born in 2008? Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.88,
      "end_seconds": 13.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Yeah, that's me. Um, hi."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.37,
      "end_seconds": 23.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "Nice to meet you, Imani. I've read your GP's letter, but I'd like to hear it from you. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.22,
      "end_seconds": 33.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "It's my knee. The right one. It's gone all swollen and, um... it just won't go down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.43,
      "end_seconds": 42.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "Swollen right knee. How long has it been like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.07,
      "end_seconds": 51.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "About three weeks? Maybe a bit more. I noticed it after games, then it just stayed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.25,
      "end_seconds": 55.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "After games, so you play sport?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.16,
      "end_seconds": 64.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Football. For school, and a Sunday team. Well, I did. I haven't, since it got bad."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.35,
      "end_seconds": 70.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Okay. Does it hurt, or is it mainly the swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.33,
      "end_seconds": 78.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "It aches. Sort of a dull... it's worse when I go down the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.39,
      "end_seconds": 87.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "So a dull ache that's worse on the stairs. Anything in the mornings?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.57,
      "end_seconds": 96.91,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "It's really stiff when I wake up. Takes ages, like an hour, before I can bend it properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.3,
      "end_seconds": 103.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "An hour of stiffness. Does it ease as the day goes on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.72,
      "end_seconds": 109.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Yeah, mostly. Then by evening it's sort of... tight again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.14,
      "end_seconds": 114.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Right. Have you noticed yourself limping?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.4,
      "end_seconds": 123.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "A bit. My mum says I walk funny. I didn't really... I hadn't noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.89,
      "end_seconds": 132.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "That's helpful, thank you. Any particular injury before it started? A fall, a twist?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.52,
      "end_seconds": 139.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. I've been thinking about it and, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.88,
      "end_seconds": 145.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Good. Any fevers, or feeling hot and shivery?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.19,
      "end_seconds": 154.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "No fever. Just tired. Really tired, actually, which I thought was revision."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.7,
      "end_seconds": 163.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Tired, yes, I'll note that. Have you had any redness or pain in your eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.74,
      "end_seconds": 168.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "No, my eyes are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.22,
      "end_seconds": 174.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "And any tummy trouble? Loose stools, belly pain, blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.17,
      "end_seconds": 179.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "No, nothing there. It's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.76,
      "end_seconds": 185.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Thanks. What medicines do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.23,
      "end_seconds": 192.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Ibuprofen, 400 mg, when the knee's bad. Mum gave me it. And, um... the cetirizine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.03,
      "end_seconds": 198.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "The cetirizine, what's that for, and what dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.77,
      "end_seconds": 207.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "For my hay fever. 10 mg, once a day, in the spring and summer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.02,
      "end_seconds": 213.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Alright. And how often is the ibuprofen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.66,
      "end_seconds": 221.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Most days now. Two, maybe, trailing off... it takes the edge off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.71,
      "end_seconds": 227.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Okay. Do you have any allergies, to medicines or food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.99,
      "end_seconds": 236.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "Peanuts. My lips went puffy and itchy once, so now I just avoid them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.72,
      "end_seconds": 247.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "Peanuts, with puffy, itchy lips. I'll put that on your record. What else is in your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.23,
      "end_seconds": 256.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "Eczema, since I was little. And acne, which is annoying. Um... and I get migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.35,
      "end_seconds": 263.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Eczema, acne and migraines, plus the hay fever. Have you had any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.18,
      "end_seconds": 271.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Tonsils out when I was six. And my appendix, two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.07,
      "end_seconds": 278.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Good. Does anyone in the family have joint or skin conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.1,
      "end_seconds": 288.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "My dad's got psoriasis. On his elbows, mostly. I don't think it's... I don't know if that's connected."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.95,
      "end_seconds": 296.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "It might well be useful to know, so thank you. Tell me about your day-to-day. School?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.03,
      "end_seconds": 307.26,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "I'm in Year 12. Doing sciences. I'm trying to keep up but the knee gets in the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.13,
      "end_seconds": 313.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "And who do you live with, and what do you eat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.97,
      "end_seconds": 321.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Mum and my little brother. And I'm vegetarian, have been since last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.68,
      "end_seconds": 340.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Great. Hop up on the couch, and I'll look at that knee."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.04,
      "end_seconds": 362.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.3,
      "text": "Your right knee is swollen and warm compared with the left. It bends only part of the way, and it's tender along the inner side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.53,
      "end_seconds": 379.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Now your numbers. Blood pressure is 112 over 68, and pulse is 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.78,
      "end_seconds": 388.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Temperature is 37.4 degrees, oxygen is 99 percent, and weight is 62 kilograms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.5,
      "end_seconds": 394.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Is that all fine? I'm sorry, I always worry about the... yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.22,
      "end_seconds": 403.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "No need to apologise. The numbers are fine, apart from the slightly warm temperature."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.65,
      "end_seconds": 409.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "So what is it? Is it something really bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.06,
      "end_seconds": 419.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "Let me explain. This looks most like an inflammatory arthritis, where the lining of the joint gets irritated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.1,
      "end_seconds": 424.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Arthritis? Like old people have?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.26,
      "end_seconds": 435.84,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "Young people get it too. I can't rule out an infection in the joint yet, which is why we test."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.3,
      "end_seconds": 441.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "An infection? That sounds scary."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.46,
      "end_seconds": 449.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "It's less likely, given the lack of fever. But we check, to be safe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 451.05,
      "end_seconds": 452.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Okay. What tests?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.53,
      "end_seconds": 464.57,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "I'd like to order blood tests for inflammation, an ultrasound scan of the knee, and an X-ray as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.13,
      "end_seconds": 480.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.38,
      "text": "The ultrasound is painless. And I'll arrange an eye check with our eye clinic, because this type of arthritis can quietly affect the eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 482.32,
      "end_seconds": 490.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks with the results, and we'll decide treatment then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 492.09,
      "end_seconds": 496.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Okay. Can I keep taking the ibuprofen until then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 499.39,
      "end_seconds": 510.31,
      "duration_seconds": 10.92,
      "text": "Yes, take it with food, and no more than you have been. We'll talk about the football after the tests."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 511.34,
      "end_seconds": 515.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Thank you. Sorry for not saying much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 518.12,
      "end_seconds": 524.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "You've told me everything I needed, Imani. Take care, and say hello to your mum."
    }
  ]
}
